<section class="pp-section" id="how">
<div class="pp-wrap">
<div class="pp-section-head">
<p class="pp-eyebrow">How it works</p>
<h2 class="pp-display pp-h-section">From 2 old outlets to 9 ports in 30 seconds</h2>
<p class="pp-lede">PlugPal uses the screw that already holds your cover plate. Swap it for the longer one in the box and the whole unit locks flat to the wall, so pulling out a plug never drags it out with it.</p>
</div>
<div class="pp-steps">
<article class="pp-step">
<div class="pp-step__num">1</div>
<h3>Take out the centre screw</h3>
{%- render 'plugpal-media', img: section.settings.img_step_1, width: 800, alt: "Screwdriver removing the cover-plate screw" -%}<div class="pp-ph"><svg class="pp-icon pp-ph__icon"><use href="#i-screw"/></svg><span class="pp-ph__text">Close-up: screwdriver on the cover-plate screw</span></div></div>
<p>Unscrew the one screw in the middle of your outlet's cover plate. The plate stays where it is.</p>
</article>
<article class="pp-step">
<div class="pp-step__num">2</div>
<h3>Plug it in</h3>
{%- render 'plugpal-media', img: section.settings.img_step_2, width: 800, alt: "PlugPal being plugged into the outlet" -%}<div class="pp-ph"><svg class="pp-icon pp-ph__icon"><use href="#i-plug"/></svg><span class="pp-ph__text">PlugPal going into the outlet, flat to the plate</span></div></div>
<p>Push PlugPal into the outlet until it sits flat against the plate. Its prongs use both sockets.</p>
</article>
<article class="pp-step">
<div class="pp-step__num">3</div>
<h3>Screw it in</h3>
{%- render 'plugpal-media', img: section.settings.img_step_3, width: 800, alt: "Long screw locking PlugPal to the wall" -%}<div class="pp-ph"><svg class="pp-icon pp-ph__icon"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span class="pp-ph__text">Long screw going through PlugPal into the box</span></div></div>
<p>Use the long screw from the box to fix it through the centre. Snug, not tight.</p>
<div class="pp-step__tip">Cheap cube adapters sag out of worn outlets. The screw is what stops that.</div>
</article>
</div>
<div class="pp-tally" aria-label="What one outlet becomes">
<div><b>5</b><span>grounded AC outlets</span></div>
<div><b>2</b><span>USB-C ports</span></div>
<div><b>2</b><span>USB-A ports</span></div>
<div><b>1</b><span>night light</span></div>
</div>
</div>
