<div class="pp-acc pp-faq" data-acc>
<div class="pp-acc__item"><button class="pp-acc__btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false">Is it safe to plug this much into one outlet?<svg class="pp-icon pp-chev"><use href="#i-down"/></svg></button>
<div class="pp-acc__panel" hidden><p>For everyday electronics, yes. PlugPal has a surge circuit, a flame-retardant housing and a screw mount that keeps it from sagging out of the wall. What matters is total load: everything shares one 15A / 1,875W circuit. Phones, lamps, TVs and a coffee maker are fine. Space heaters and pairs of heat appliances go straight into the wall.</p></div></div>
<div class="pp-acc__item"><button class="pp-acc__btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false">Will it fit my outlet?<svg class="pp-icon pp-chev"><use href="#i-down"/></svg></button>
<div class="pp-acc__panel" hidden><p>It fits standard US and Canadian two-socket, 3-prong grounded outlets with a centre screw in the cover plate. Deep plates may need the longer 6-32 screw, which is in the box.</p></div></div>
<div class="pp-acc__item"><button class="pp-acc__btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false">My outlets are 2-prong. Will it work?<svg class="pp-icon pp-chev"><use href="#i-down"/></svg></button>
<div class="pp-acc__panel" hidden><p>No. PlugPal has a 3-prong grounded plug, so it needs a 3-prong outlet. Older homes often have 2-prong outlets in some rooms, so check before you order.</p></div></div>
<div class="pp-acc__item"><button class="pp-acc__btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false">Does it block the light switch or the other socket?<svg class="pp-icon pp-chev"><use href="#i-down"/></svg></button>
<div class="pp-acc__panel" hidden><p>It covers both sockets of the outlet and turns them into nine ports. On a combined switch-and-outlet plate it sits beside the switch. <span class="pp-verify">Add the exact dimensions from your sample here.</span></p></div></div>
<div class="pp-acc__item"><button class="pp-acc__btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false">Will the USB-C port charge my laptop?<svg class="pp-icon pp-chev"><use href="#i-down"/></svg></button>
<div class="pp-acc__panel" hidden><p>No. The USB ports are for phones, earbuds, watches and controllers. They share their power, so charging slows a little when all four are in use. Laptops and large tablets need their own charger, which you can plug into one of the five AC outlets.</p></div></div>
<div class="pp-acc__item"><button class="pp-acc__btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false">Is the night light bright enough? Does it stay on all night?<svg class="pp-icon pp-chev"><use href="#i-down"/></svg></button>
<div class="pp-acc__panel" hidden><p>It's a soft glow made for hallways, bathrooms and nurseries, not a room light. The sensor turns it on at dusk and off when the room gets light. <span class="pp-verify">Tap the light icon to set the brightness.</span></p></div></div>
<div class="pp-acc__item"><button class="pp-acc__btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false">Do I need an electrician?<svg class="pp-icon pp-chev"><use href="#i-down"/></svg></button>
<div class="pp-acc__panel" hidden><p>No. There's no wiring. You need a flat-head or Phillips screwdriver and about 30 seconds.</p></div></div>
<div class="pp-acc__item"><button class="pp-acc__btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false">I rent. Can I use it?<svg class="pp-icon pp-chev"><use href="#i-down"/></svg></button>
<div class="pp-acc__panel" hidden><p>Yes. It doesn't change your wiring and it leaves no marks. When you move, unscrew it, put your old cover-plate screw back and take PlugPal with you.</p></div></div>
<div class="pp-acc__item"><button class="pp-acc__btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false">My outlet is loose. Will PlugPal hold it?<svg class="pp-icon pp-chev"><use href="#i-down"/></svg></button>
<div class="pp-acc__panel" hidden><p>No, and you shouldn't try. If an outlet is loose, cracked, sunken into the wall or won't hold a screw, have it repaired first. PlugPal needs a solid outlet.</p></div></div>
<div class="pp-acc__item"><button class="pp-acc__btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false">How long does the surge protection last?<svg class="pp-icon pp-chev"><use href="#i-down"/></svg></button>
<div class="pp-acc__panel" hidden><p>Surge protection is rated in joules, and each big surge uses some of it up. The protected-indicator light shows it's still working. If the light goes out, the outlets still work but surge protection doesn't, so replace the unit.</p></div></div>
<div class="pp-acc__item"><button class="pp-acc__btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false">Why not buy a $12 one from Amazon?<svg class="pp-icon pp-chev"><use href="#i-down"/></svg></button>
<div class="pp-acc__panel" hidden><p>Many cheap extenders list joule ratings that don't match their own boxes, and some don't screw in at all. PlugPal publishes its <span class="pp-verify">certification and joule rating</span>, includes the long screw and load guide, and comes with a 30-day guarantee and real support.</p></div></div>
<div class="pp-acc__item"><button class="pp-acc__btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false">Does it work in my country?<svg class="pp-icon pp-chev"><use href="#i-down"/></svg></button>
<div class="pp-acc__panel" hidden><p>PlugPal is made for US and Canadian outlets (Type B, 120V). It won't fit outlets in the UK, Europe or Australia.</p></div></div>
<div class="pp-acc__item"><button class="pp-acc__btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false">What's your guarantee?<svg class="pp-icon pp-chev"><use href="#i-down"/></svg></button>
<div class="pp-acc__panel" hidden><p>30 days. If it doesn't fit or you're not happy, contact us for a refund. Faulty night lights or USB ports are replaced.</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
